# Line endings are pinned explicitly rather than left to each clone's local
# git config (core.autocrlf) - a Windows user's default "checkout
# Windows-style" setting is harmless for .ps1 (PowerShell reads both LF and
# CRLF) but would be actively wrong for .sh: a CRLF shebang line
# (`#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`) makes bash/macOS refuse to run the script at all.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.sh text eol=lf
